From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 04:20:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 118/225] arm64: dts: sprd: add ums512 display pipeline; port
 ROCKNIX panel driver

Port the display SoC nodes into ums512.dtsi: dpu/iommu_disp/dsi (under a
mm simple-bus), the display-subsystem node, pwm, and the dphy fixed
clocks. On the RG Rotate board, un-stage the framebuffer reserved-memory
+ simple-fb, pwm-backlight, lcd avdd/avee regulators, and the panel@0
"rocknix,generic-dsi" node with its full init sequence.

Port the out-of-tree ROCKNIX panel-generic-dsi driver (DRM_PANEL_GENERIC_DSI)
into 7.1; it builds as-is bar an explicit linux/hex.h include for hex2bin.
The upstream sprd DRM stack (dpu/dsi/drm/gem/megacores) compiles cleanly
against 7.1. Enable DRM_SPRD, the panel, PWM_SPRD, BACKLIGHT_PWM.

NOTE: the load-bearing free-run / prepare_prev_first cold-init driver
hacks (sprd_dpu.c DPI_HALT cleared, sprd_dsi.c DSI_MODE_CFG=0) are NOT yet
re-applied on top of the clean upstream drivers; without them the panel is
expected to blank on this board. Re-apply + on-device validation pending.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
